OL,3,AAdvisor O'Neill rules out government
OL,4,Ajob but backs PM's devolution plans
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe economist Lord Jim O'Neill, who has
OL,7,Fbeen advising the prime minister, has
OL,8,Fsaid he will not be taking a job in
OL,9,FAndy Burnham's government.
OL,11,FLord O'Neill, a crossbench peer, was
OL,12,Fonce a treasury minister under the
OL,13,FConservatives.
OL,15,FAs first reported by, external the
OL,16,FFinancial Times, he said he did not
OL,17,Fwant the constraints involved in taking
OL,18,Fon a formal role.
OL,20,FThe former chief economist at Goldman
OL,21,FSachs had been tipped to become
OL,22,FBurnham's chief economic adviser.
OL,23,APub: 22-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
